from ./Selection import Selecting, Selection

export abstract anchor ReadinessThreshold extends Selection as readiness-threshold:
    description:: string
    minExplicitness:: null:: number: null
    minResolutionRate:: null:: number: null
    minCompleteness:: null:: number: null
    maxAmbiguityRate:: null:: number: null
    maxImplementationFreedom:: null:: number: null
    maxContradictions:: number: 0

export anchor Readiness:
    description:
        Implementation-ready is the point where a specification leaves an
        implementer nothing meaningful to invent. It is not a claim that the
        specification is perfect. It is a line a project draws: below it,
        more should be written before anyone builds; above it, building can
        start.

    theDefaultLine:
        With no threshold configured, an entity is ready only when it has no
        open items of any kind and every expectation's question is answered.
        That is strict on purpose: it means nothing is left to decide.

    drawingYourOwn:
        A project draws its own lines with readiness thresholds, each applied
        to the entities it selects, as described in @{Selecting}. A threshold
        sets a minimum or maximum for any measure; a limit left null is not
        checked. Contradictions are never allowed unless a threshold says so,
        because building from a contradiction means implementing one side of
        it at random.

        ```piton
        // readiness-threshold comes from the analysis module. It is declared here only so
        // that this example compiles on its own.
        abstract anchor ReadinessThreshold as readiness-threshold:
            description:: string
            paths:: string[]: []
            minCompleteness:: null:: number: null
            maxImplementationFreedom:: null:: number: null

        readiness-threshold ShapeReady:
            description: Components can be built with a little freedom left.
            paths:
                - spec/shape/**
            minCompleteness: 0.9
            maxImplementationFreedom: 0.1
        ```

        An entity selected by more than one threshold must meet all of them.

    theResult:
        Each entity is reported as ready or not ready, and when it is not,
        every limit it fails is listed with its value. A whole scope is ready
        when every entity in it is.
